# What must never be baked into an image.
#
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so without this file the image would
# carry the development database, the uploads in it, and - worst - the key that
# signs session cookies. An image is pushed to a registry and pulled by anyone
# who can reach it; a key inside one is a key given away.

# Keys and provider credentials. These belong on the running machine only, and
# are generated there on first start if absent.
.secret
.data_key
.vapid_keys
.ref_keys
.smtp_config
.stripe_key
.qtsp_config
.eid_config
.ai_config
seam.env

# The database and everything uploaded into it. These live on the mounted
# volume at /data, not in the image.
seam.db
seam.db-wal
seam.db-shm
uploads/
backups/

# Local Python, never the right build for the image's base.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Not needed at runtime, and they make the image bigger and the build slower.
tests/
marketing/
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
!DEPLOY.md
